        "explanation": "A. Add a human review and approval step before making decisions that affect the staff’s financial situation. — Correct\nMicrosoft's Respo nsible AI principles emphasize accountability and human oversight. Because sentimentanalysis results will directly affect employees' bonuses, a human should review and approve the decision rather than allowing an automated system to make the financial decision by itself.\nB. Include the Sentiment Analysis results when surveys return a low confidence score. — Incorrect Low-confidence results are less reliable. Using them to calculate bonuses could lead to inaccurate or unfair financial decisions. Low-confidence predictions should generally be reviewed or excluded rather than automatically used.\n\nC. Use all the surveys, including surveys by customers who requested that their account be deleted and their data be removed. — Incorrect\nThis conflicts with privacy and data governance principles. If customers have requested deletion of their data, their deleted data should not continue to be used for this purpose.\nD. Publish the raw survey data to a central location and provide the staff with access to the location. — Incorrect\nMaking raw survey data broadly accessible can expose personal or sensitive customer information and violates the principle of protecting privacy and security. Access should be appropriately restricted. Final Answer\nA. Add a human review and approval step before making decisions that affect the staff’s financial situation."
