        "explanation": "A. Tool call — Correct\nThe requirement is to prevent Agent1 from sending content tagged as Violence to the MCP server. The tool call intervention point occurs immediately before the agent sends a request to an external tool or MCP server. A guardrail at this point can inspect the content and block the call if it is tagged as Violence.\nB. User input — Incorrect\nThe user input intervention point checks content coming directly from the user. The requirement is specifically to prevent content from being sent to the MCP server, which happens during the tool call.\nC. Tool response — Incorrect\nThe tool response intervention point examines data returned by the MCP server. It does not prevent content from being sent to the server.\nD. Output — Incorrect\nThe output intervention point checks the agent's final response before it is presented to the user. It occurs after the MCP interaction and therefore cannot prevent the content from being sent to the MCP server.\n\nFinal Answer\nA. Tool call"
