      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "text": "Add a reflection pass before the responses are returned.",
        "explanation": "A. Add a reflection pass before the responses are returned. — Correct\nA reflection pass allows the agent to review its generated response against the retrieved policy documents before returning it. It can identify missing information, omissions, or incomplete parts and improve the response. This directly addresses the requirement to improve response completeness in the application logic before returning the response.\nB. Enable response streaming. — Incorrect\nResponse streaming controls how the response is delivered to the application or user. It does not review or improve the completeness of the generated summary.\nC. Increase the value of the presence_penalty parameter. — Incorrect presence_penalty influences whether the model is encouraged to introduce new topics or tokens rather than repeating existing content. It is not a mechanism for checking whether a response is complete.\nD. Decrease the value of the max_tokens parameter. — Incorrect max_tokens controls the maximum amount of tokens that can be generated. Decreasing it can actually limit the length of the response, potentially making completeness worse.\nFinal Answer\nA. Add a reflection pass before the responses are returned."
      },
      "explanation": "A. Add a reflection pass before the responses are returned. — Correct\nA reflection pass allows the agent to review its generated response against the retrieved policy documents before returning it. It can identify missing information, omissions, or incomplete parts and improve the response. This directly addresses the requirement to improve response completeness in the application logic before returning the response.\nB. Enable response streaming. — Incorrect\nResponse streaming controls how the response is delivered to the application or user. It does not review or improve the completeness of the generated summary.\nC. Increase the value of the presence_penalty parameter. — Incorrect presence_penalty influences whether the model is encouraged to introduce new topics or tokens rather than repeating existing content. It is not a mechanism for checking whether a response is complete.\nD. Decrease the value of the max_tokens parameter. — Incorrect max_tokens controls the maximum amount of tokens that can be generated. Decreasing it can actually limit the length of the response, potentially making completeness worse.\nFinal Answer\nA. Add a reflection pass before the responses are returned."
