        "explanation": "Here's a structured technical justification for the correct answer in paragraph and bullet point format, followed by explanations for why other options are less suitable:\nRecommended Service: C. Azure AI Custom Vision\nJustification for Azure AI Custom Vision:\nAzure AI Custom Vision is the most suitable service for this scenario due to the following key reasons:\nDefective Product Identification in Real-Time Video Feed: While Custom Vision primarily processes images, it can be integrated with a video processing pipeline where frames from the video feed are extracted and analyzed as individual images. This approach enables the identification of defective products in near real-time. Training with Image Library: Custom Vision excels at training models from user-provided image datasets, which aligns perfectly with the requirement of leveraging an existing library of approved and rejected product images for model training.\nMinimized Development Effort: The service provides a user-friendly interface and SDKs for easy integration, reducing the development effort required for training, deploying, and maintaining the model compared to more general-purpose machine learning platforms.\nWhy Other Options are Less Suitable:\nA. Azure Vision in Foundry Tools:\nMisconception: \"Azure Vision\" is not a recognized standalone service by Microsoft Azure in the context provided. If referring to computer vision capabilities within Azure, Custom Vision or Cognitive Services' Computer Vision would be more accurate.\nFoundry Tools are not directly related to the described requirements, as they pertain more to data integration and transformation rather than AI/ML model training and deployment for image/video analysis.\nB. Azure AI Video Indexer:\nPrimary Function: Designed for video indexing, search, and analytics (e.g., people, text, objects detection in a more general sense), not specifically tailored for custom defect detection based on a user-provided dataset.\n\nModel Training: Not optimized for training a custom model with a specific image library for defect detection.\nD. Azure Machine Learning:\nSuitability: While capable of handling the task, it requires significantly more development effort, expertise in machine learning model selection, training, and deployment, which contradicts the \"Minimizes Development Effort\" requirement.\nCustomization and Control: Provides too much of both for this specific use case where a more streamlined, dedicated computer vision solution is preferable.\nReferences\nAzure Custom Vision Documentation\nComparing Azure Services for Computer Vision Tasks"
